        "topic": "Partial Fractions",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2024",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume the partial fraction decomposition is:<br><br>$\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$<br><br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x - 2)$:<br>$3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$<br><br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = 2$:<br>For $x = -1$: $3(-1) + 5 = A(-1 - 2) + B(0)$<br>$-3 + 5 = -3A$<br>$2 = -3A$<br>$A = -\\frac{2}{3}$<br><br>For $x = 2$: $3(2) + 5 = A(0) + B(2 + 1)$<br>$6 + 5 = 3B$<br>$11 = 3B$<br>$B = \\frac{11}{3}$<br><br>Thus, the partial fractions are:<br>$\\frac{-2/3}{x + 1} + \\frac{11/3}{x - 2}$</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
