        "topic": "Differentiation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2024",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the derivative of $y = x^3 \\ln x$ with respect to $x$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the product rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}[u \\cdot v] = u'v + uv'$, where $u = x^3$ and $v = \\ln x$.<br><br>$u' = 3x^2$<br>$v' = \\frac{1}{x}$<br><br>Thus, $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 \\ln x + x^3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} = 3x^2 \\ln x + x^2$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
